# Keep the build context lean and secret-free (plan F6-T1).
#
# At the repository root, not beside the Containerfile, and that is the only placement that works.
# Every builder `deploy/jenkins/lib/image.sh` supports — docker, buildah, podman, kaniko — reads the
# ignore file from the **root of the build context**, and both call sites pass the repository root
# as the context (`.github/workflows/image.yml`, `image.sh`'s `build_and_push`). BuildKit alone also
# honours `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, so `deploy/Containerfile.dockerignore` would tidy this next to
# the Containerfile and leave three of the four builders ignoring it. It lived at `deploy/` for a
# long time, where nothing reads one at all: the context was the whole 6.9 GB tree, `.venv` and
# `.git` included, uploaded to a shared builder under kaniko.
.git
.github
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
tests
docs
*.md
!README.md
.env
*.pem
*.key
